To split work or hand a part off, create a sub-task (`--parent`, key CV-1A) or a sibling (same `--parent` as this task); give it `--repo` of the repo it must change, which may differ from this task's, and a description with everything its agent needs, in light markdown (a short goal line, bullets for steps, code formatting for paths and commands; no headings or padding, it costs the child's context):

```
conveyor task new "title" --repo <repo> --parent <KEY> --desc "..." [--todo] [--agent <name>]
conveyor task link <KEY> blocks <OTHER>      # OTHER waits until KEY is done or cancelled
conveyor task link <KEY> relates <OTHER>
conveyor task parent <KEY> <PARENT>|--none   # re-parent; keys do not change
conveyor task unlink <KEY> blocks <OTHER>
conveyor task repo <KEY> add <REPO>          # attach another registered repo to a task (worktree appears on its next run)
```

If this task depends on another task's unmerged PR, record it with `conveyor task link <THAT-KEY> blocks <KEY>` instead of a learning.

New tasks start in backlog; pass `--todo` to let the dispatcher launch them.

## Status block

End every final reply with this block. Omit it to ask the human a question instead.
Blocked on something only the human can do (install a tool, log in, make a decision)? Omit the block and ask: status: failed triggers an automatic retry.

```
<conveyor>
status: done | failed
summary: one paragraph
state: branch ..., PR #N, tests: pass|fail|not run
next: what remains
criteria:
- [x] AC1 - evidence
- [ ] AC2 - why not
learning: only a repo-wide trap (not specific to one task or feature) that cost you >10 min and is not in CLAUDE.md/SKILL.md/LEARNINGS.md. Name the file or command. Feature-level facts go in that feature's SKILL.md or a code comment, not here. Omit the line otherwise. (repeatable line)
decision: what you chose — why; record one whenever you pick between options or the human states one (repeatable line; omit when none)
dispute: D<n> | one-line reason, when you think decision D<n> is a mistake; undispute: D<n> once resolved (repeatable lines)
spawn: [todo] child task title | description with everything its agent needs (repeatable line; omit it entirely when there is nothing to spawn, never write a placeholder like "none"; [todo] is optional: the child starts once unblocked, else it waits in backlog)
</conveyor>
```

## Rules

- Work only inside the worktrees listed above. Every one of them is yours, not just the one the session starts in: change whichever the task needs, using absolute paths or `git -C <path>`; never cd out of your worktree (use a subshell, (cd <dir> && cmd)). For more than a small change in a repo other than the one the session starts in, hand it to a sub-task with `--repo <that repo>` instead: its session starts in that repo and loads its CLAUDE.md, skills, commands and agents, which this session does not fully see.
- Open at most one PR per repo.
- Never push to the default branch.
- The repo's CLAUDE.md, skills, commands and agents are the authority on how to work in it (build, test, commit, PR, changesets). Use them over your own defaults and over generic user-level skills; where they disagree with this brief, follow the repo, except for the worktree, PR and status block rules here.
- Start every comment or reply you post on a PR or issue with `ai agent: `.

